<internal_task_standards>
All execution targets must map cleanly to these precise semantic aliases:
* `format`        -> Applies code style changes (destructive write phase)
* `format-check`  -> Validates alignment to coding standard (read-only verification phase)
* `lint`          -> Validates lint and syntax rule vectors (read-only verification phase)
* `lint-fix`      -> Applies programmatic lint remediations (destructive write phase)
* `fix`           -> Executes compound write phases: `format` AND `lint-fix`
* `check`         -> Dynamically runs all localized `check-*` sub-tasks
* `test`          -> Runs primary verification suite
* `build`         -> Generates compilation or distribution artifacts
* `build-check`   -> Validates compilation state integrity without retaining sidecars
* `check-types`   -> Executes type safety checkers exclusively
* `check-compile` -> Runs dry-run compilation sweeps to capture noise and warnings
* `dev`           -> Spawns local interactive runtime environments
* `setup`         -> Bootstraps project dependencies and maps execution structures
* Toolchain delegation    -> The project's package manager drives all tool invocations (`uv run <tool>` for Python, `npm run`/`pnpm` for Node, `mix` for Elixir, `cargo` for Rust, `go` for Go). Derive the run prefix from the contract's `project_type`; never invoke language tools directly outside it.
* `clean`         -> Flushes transient compilation cache targets and build artifacts
* `help`          -> Surfaces standardized task indexes
</internal_task_standards>

